Description:

Malformed credentials in an HTTP Authorization header are now rejected before
their parameters are read.  Previously a parameter list that ended in a
separator -- a bare trailing comma, for instance -- or that named a parameter
with an empty value caused the parser to walk past the end of the string
holding the credentials and read whatever heap memory followed it.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-387x-mcqp-xrw8.


